		{"id":"cc9c75f606b29066","type":"text","text":"# Stimulus\n- The idea/concept (abstract) that the sender has and would like to convey\n","isStartNode":false,"x":-1149,"y":-145,"width":295,"height":192},
		{"id":"07af9c3c43c4aca0","type":"text","text":"# Encoding\nThe sender encodes the message into words or other channels.","x":-776,"y":-152,"width":318,"height":204},
		{"id":"9fe02a7f1f1027bc","type":"text","text":"# Decoding\nThe receiver receives the message and decodes/interprets it.","x":-381,"y":-152,"width":302,"height":204},
		{"id":"c5c98a96d62ac81a","type":"text","text":"# Feedback (optional)\nIf the receiver chooses to respond, he/she will provide feedback (the receiver becomes the sender).\n\nHowever, this is optional and depends on the [[Models of Communication]] used. \n\nIf the receiver decides to send their feedback, they become the sender (process restarts).","x":-7,"y":-199,"width":441,"height":298},
